cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Evidence Gap Radar: live PubMed evidence-gap mapping"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Latif
    given-names: Tajamal
    affiliation: "Islamabad, Pakistan"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-05
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tjkawish/evidence-gap-radar"
url: "https://tjkawish.github.io/evidence-gap-radar/"
abstract: >-
  A browser-based tool that crosses a research topic with two user-defined
  axes (for example countries and study designs), counts PubMed records for
  every combination, compares each count with its expected value under
  independence, and flags under-studied combinations using a Poisson z-score.
  Flagged cells can be checked against OpenAlex and Google Scholar.
keywords:
  - evidence gap map
  - PubMed
  - bibliometrics
  - systematic review
  - public health
  - research prioritisation
